  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "The flow in one line each",
      "items": [
        "1 Connect: a live Connection to PostgreSQL, SQL Server, MySQL/MariaDB or Oracle, or a schema file; DAWAM stores the schema as a Snapshot.",
        "2 Documents: upload SDAs, specs and images; DAWAM parses, OCRs and indexes them for search.",
        "3 Understand: browse the Source Schema and its ER diagram, profile columns, scan for PII, accept or reject inferred relationships.",
        "4 KPIs: build the KPI catalog and link KPIs to source columns.",
        "5 Design: staging is generated automatically; Core and Mart are designed by hand or proposed by the AI, with validated mappings and lineage.",
        "6 Evaluate: a rule-based score per Layer with an approval gate, an advisory AI evaluation, then DDL and a documentation pack."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "The AI assistant",
      "items": [
        "A chat panel available at every step, acting with the user's permissions; the dashed arrows show what it reads or proposes at each step.",
        "It answers from DAWAM's real data through tools: search_documents (RAG), describe_image, get_profile, run_source_query (guarded, PII-masked), suggest_kpis, generate_dw_schema, draft_mappings, evaluate_dw, render_diagram.",
        "Nothing it produces is applied directly: changes arrive as Change Sets the user reviews; evaluation findings never feed the score.",
        "See the AI architecture diagrams for the loop, the LLM gateway and RAG."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Diagrams the product draws",
      "items": [
        "Source ER diagram: tables of the latest Snapshot with accepted relationships and PII markers (SourceErDiagram.tsx).",
        "Warehouse: star diagram and bus matrix per Layer (diagrams/StarDiagram.tsx, BusMatrix.tsx), lineage graph (LineageGraph.tsx).",
        "In chat: render_diagram draws the star schema or lineage as Mermaid from DAWAM's model, not from the model's memory."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Simplified",
      "items": [
        "Steps are not strictly ordered: the flow shows the usual order. A source change re-runs steps 1, 3 and 5 through Change Sets and propagation.",
        "Background jobs (extraction, profiling, PII scan, inference, indexing) run in the worker; see the job lifecycle diagram.",
        "Stage 4 of the README, DW Implementation (dbt, SQL transforms), is a next phase with no code and is not shown."
      ]
    }
  ]
